// openclaw.json candidate: ACP policy fix — allowedAgents correction
// Target: /etc/openclaw/openclaw.json
// Date: 2026-03-26
// Prerequisite: Phase 4 maintenance window completed (2026-03-25)
// Root cause analysis: docs/planning/acp-policy-fix-analysis.md
//
// DELTA candidate — only changed fields shown.
// Apply by editing the live openclaw.json.
// ESCALATION: This changes /etc/openclaw/openclaw.json.
//
// === ROOT CAUSE ===
//
// Error: "ACP agent "claude-engineer" is not allowed by policy."
//
// The acp.allowedAgents field controls which ACP harness IDs (e.g., "claude",
// "codex", "gemini") are allowed — NOT OpenClaw agent IDs (e.g., "claude-engineer").
//
// When main agent calls sessions_spawn(runtime: "acp", agentId: "claude-engineer"),
// the system treats "claude-engineer" as an ACP harness ID and checks it against
// allowedAgents: ["claude"]. Since "claude-engineer" != "claude", it fails.
//
// Source code evidence (pi-embedded-CbCYZxIb.js:6283-6290):
//   function isAcpAgentAllowedByPolicy(cfg, agentId) {
//     const allowed = (cfg.acp?.allowedAgents ?? []).map(entry => normalizeAgentId(entry));
//     if (allowed.length === 0) return true;  // empty = allow all
//     return allowed.includes(normalizeAgentId(agentId));
//   }
//
// === FIX ===
//
// Remove allowedAgents (or set to []) so the empty-array-allows-all path is taken.
// The acp.defaultAgent: "claude" already constrains the default harness.
// Adding "claude-engineer" to allowedAgents would be wrong conceptually — it's not
// an ACP harness, it's an OpenClaw agent.
//
// Additionally, ensure main agent's workspace guidance tells it to use
// agentId: "claude" (the ACP harness ID) when spawning ACP sessions.
{
  acp: {
    enabled: true,
    dispatch: {
      enabled: true,
    },
    defaultAgent: "claude",
    // REMOVED: allowedAgents: ["claude"],
    // Reason: empty/absent = allow all ACP harnesses.
    // The defaultAgent field already sets the default.
    // If we want to restrict, use: allowedAgents: ["claude"]
    // BUT then main agent must use agentId: "claude" (not "claude-engineer")
    // when calling sessions_spawn(runtime: "acp").
    maxConcurrentSessions: 2,
    stream: {
      coalesceIdleMs: 300,
      maxChunkChars: 1200,
    },
    runtime: {
      ttlMinutes: 60,
      // NOTE: permissionMode is NOT a valid field here in 2026.3.23-2.
      // The acp.runtime schema only accepts: ttlMinutes, installCommand.
      // Permission is controlled via Claude Code's ~/.claude/settings.json
      // (already deployed at /var/lib/openclaw/.claude/settings.json with
      // full allow list) and the acpx backend's built-in config.
    },
  },

  // Also ensure plugins.allow includes host-ops-tool (currently deployed)
  // and does NOT include "acpx" (not needed in 2026.3.22+).
  plugins: {
    allow: ["feishu", "host-ops-tool"],
    // No acpx entry needed — ACP is in core for 2026.3.22+
  },
}
